The answer is: ...came to a cabin in the woods. The cabin belonged to a man named Ishkodi. Ishkodi was sitting by the fire when the two men came in. The men were from a neighboring clan. They were on a mission to kill Ishkodi because he had killed one of theirs. Ishkodi was a great archer and he knew that the men were coming for him. He had prepared for their arrival. He told his wife Tantali to hide their son Sasee. Sasee was only one year old. Tantali took the baby and hid him under some leaves in a pit in the ground. Ishkodi told his wife to tell the men that he was not there. She did as he told her. The men searched for him but he was not there. They left the cabin and went back to their clan. Ishkodi came out of the cabin after they had left. He went to a tree and climbed up into it. He made himself a smoking pipe and smoked. He was thinking that perhaps he should leave the area for a while. As he sat there smoking, the ground beneath him gave way and he fell into a pit. It was a trap that the men from the neighboring clan had prepared for him. He broke his leg in the fall. The men came back to the cabin while he was there. They found him in the pit and killed him. They took his body back to their cabin and burned it. Sasee was later found by a woman named Katus. She took him in and raised him as her own.


