The answer is: ...came to a cabin in the forest. The night was quiet and the only sound was the snoring of the two men. Suddenly, there was a rustling in the bushes outside the cabin. One man jumped up and went to the window to investigate. It was his brother, returning from his nightly hunt. He had forgotten his key and was going to enter the cabin through the window. The man at the window fired upon his brother, thinking him to be a bear. What happened (in detail)? [/INST] The answer is: The brother fell to the ground, dead. The man at the window was horrified at what he had done. He went outside and dug a grave in the forest, and then went back to the cabin and spent the night weeping by the fire. 
From the book "Tales of the North" by Rev. F. M. Densmore.


