Their dance was strange and strange was the music they made.
One night two men from Egulac...

Their heads were wrapped in yellow hide;
Their bodies were smeared with red paint;
On their faces they wore the likeness of the moon;
And in their hands they held their rattles of bone.

The women watched from the house and the children hid;
The men from Egulac were feared in those days.
The dance was strange and the music was strange;
And the two men continued to dance and to sing:

"We are the two men from Egulac,
We come to dance for you.
We are the two men from Egulac,
